NOTE ON DATA LICENSING

The MIT license above covers the SOURCE CODE in this repository
(build_red_hill_model.py, stage1_grids.py, index.html and the viewer).

The DATA products are licensed separately:

  Elevation, terrain, structures and stockpile geometry are derived from
  USGS 3DEP LiDAR (project CO_SanLuisJuanMiguel_2020_D20), which is in the
  PUBLIC DOMAIN as a work of the United States Government.

  Road, rail and drainage alignments are derived from OpenStreetMap,
  (c) OpenStreetMap contributors, licensed under the Open Database License
  (ODbL) v1.0: https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/

  ODbL requires attribution and share-alike for derived databases. If you
  redistribute or build on the OSM-derived linework, you must credit
  OpenStreetMap contributors and license the derived database under ODbL.

No Google Maps imagery, Street View, or Photorealistic 3D Tiles data was used
in producing this model.
